			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add atomic service barrel exports for all VS Code services\n\nAdd 21 new barrel files under Source/Effect/ that re-export the full public surface from each atomic service directory (Commands, Decorations, Editor, Extensions, Files, History, Keybinding, Label, Language, Lifecycle, Model, Notification, Output, Progress, QuickInput, Search, Storage, Terminal, TextFile, TextModelResolver, Themes, WorkingCopy, Workspaces).\n\nUpdate Source/Effect/index.ts to re-export from all named barrels, providing a cleaner public API surface where consumers can import directly from the barrel (e.g., `./Commands.js`) rather than reaching into the subdirectory (e.g., `./Commands/Live.js`).\n\nThis enables more organized imports and prevents symbol list drift between the barrel and the service implementation.",
